-- road_cut.lua: generated by Art/Studio/Regions/Lindenmoor/road_cut.py from road_cut.lua.tmpl. Do not edit by hand.
-- Lindenmoor road cutting (Ruling 31): the expansion ground under the north-east road (LindenmoorExpansion.Travel,
-- built by setup.lua) is regraded so its top meets the road's underside (y 6) and blends back to the ground around.
-- Run in Studio EDIT, Ye only, never in Play:  python -I Art/Tools/rbxc.py luau "placeId: 106992859583940" Edit @road_cut.lua
-- MODE:
--   "apply": refuses if LindenmoorRoadCut is set, the backup RenseiBackups["Pre-RoadCut_2026-10-24"] exists, the seam
--            regrade and seam_pits are not applied (the plan is computed on top of them), or any part it replaces is
--            not exactly where the plan says. Then, in a pcall that undoes everything on an error (ChangeHistory-
--            recorded when Studio allows it): rebuilds the changed ground (Top/Side clones of the parts they replace,
--            attribute LindenmoorRoadCutNew; originals to the backup, tags in RegionKitTags, old path in
--            LindenmoorRoadCutPath, ObjectValue LindenmoorRoadCutParent); moves objects standing on a changed cell
--            (not under the road) by its height change (old CFrame in LindenmoorRoadCutFrom); then runs the checks.
--            The road and its travel pieces (Ground slabs, Passage legs, RoadPoints, Threshold, Encounters, the
--            RoadStart arrival, the RoadGate arch) are never touched.
--   "undo":  reverses all of it. Nothing is planned after it. While it is applied, seam_pits.lua, gorge_fix.lua and
--            regrade_seam.lua refuse to undo, and import/restore.lua refuses to run; bed_fix.lua's bedundo,
--            shelters.lua and east_west_names.lua don't check it.
--            Rollback order: east_west_names, shelters, road_cut, bed, seam_pits, gorge, regrade, restore.lua, prep_ye.
--   "check": the checks only: RoadPoints vs the ground under them, a hollow under any road column, the ground tops
--            as planned, the bare-Baseplate scan, moved objects' bases, the part count, route steps.
--   "test":  snapshot, apply, checks, undo, snapshot.
